# AI assistant working notes (local only, never published).
# Bare `CLAUDE.md` at the root is the intended one; the `**/` pattern is because
# a `mirobody/pulse/CLAUDE.md` was committed once and shipped to PyPI inside the
# wheel — an internal notes file, under a filename that tells open-source
# readers to skip it. Its content was real module documentation and now lives at
# mirobody/pulse/README.md.
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md

# Internal notes — LOCAL ONLY, deliberately. One directory, one rule.
#
# Our own measurements are not what an open-source reader needs. What they need
# is a demo they can run (`examples/`) and a claim they can check themselves
# (`pytest mirobody/test_engine_coverage.py -s` prints the published score). The
# rule for which side a number falls on: backed by a test in the repo that
# anyone can run -> publishable; produced by `eval/` -> not.
#
# The same rule sorts prose. `internal/` holds what is addressed to US:
# `internal-testing.md` (our measurements), `library-surface-feedback.md` (a
# defect list against our own release), `frontend-shipping.md` (a gap/bug
# inventory of the current setup). A defect list is not documentation an
# outside reader needs handed to them, and `docs/` is published.
#
# These used to be three separate decisions in three places, and only one of
# them worked: `internal-testing.md` was ignored, while `frontend-shipping.md`
# sat in `docs/` and shipped, and the header of `internal-testing.md` claimed
# "Gitignored on purpose" for a rule that covered only itself. One directory
# now, so the question is never asked per file again.
internal/

# Resolver evaluation harness — the DATA is local only, the RUNNER is not.
#
# The two used to be one decision and they are not the same thing. The test set
# is derived in part from a sibling private repo's curated seed, and a
# published benchmark shipped alongside the thing it grades is an invitation to
# tune against it — so `testset.jsonl`, `build_testset.py` and every
# timestamped result stay out.
#
# `run_eval.py` ships, and only it. It is the part other people need and cannot
# write for themselves: it defines the four metrics, the analyte-level grading
# rule and the strata, and it takes `--testset <path>`, so a downstream team can
# grade the same resolver against their own distribution without their cases
# ever reaching this repository. A harness nobody else can run is not a shared
# harness.
#
# `README.md` stays out with the data: it names the set's provenance and prints
# per-stratum result tables, both of which are exactly the "not a public claim"
# half. The runner's own docstring carries what a user of it needs.
eval/*
!eval/run_eval.py

# Local regression suite. Not published: the repository keeps only the tests
# that are evidence for something it claims (see [tool.pytest.ini_options] in
# pyproject.toml). Everything else lives here so it can be thorough without
# being public API.
/tests/
